I implemented `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, following the existing pattern for derived read-only owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipNumber`).

Two hand-edited files:

1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema. This is the source of truth for the build-generated `OwnerDto`, so the field appears in the response DTO automatically.

2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — added `@Mapping(target = "contactPreference", expression = "java(contactPreference(owner))")` plus a small single-responsibility helper:
   ```java
   default String contactPreference(Owner owner) {
       String email = owner.getEmail();
       return email != null && !email.isBlank() ? "EMAIL" : "PHONE";
   }
   ```

Because the logic lives in the mapper, every owner responder (`GET`, create, update, list) picks it up with no duplication — no changes needed to the `Owner` entity, the OfficeFloor YAML, or the response functions. Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.

